Licences and provenance of the C test corpus
============================================

`tinycc/` and `pp_tcc/` are the inputs `toyos-cc` is tested against. Most of
them are not ours. This file says which, and carries the notices that have to
travel with them; it is the attribution the corpus was missing until
2026-08-08.

They are *data* — source files a compiler under test reads and a guest then
runs — and nothing here is linked into ToyOS. That is why an LGPL-2.1 corpus
does not put its terms on this repository's own MIT OR Apache-2.0 code. It is
not why they may be carried unattributed, which is a separate obligation and
the one this file discharges.


What is whose
-------------

Established by content, not by memory: every file was compared byte for byte
against tinycc upstream at 64552b3faa39ee7948a9ea21bfcc11045b90c70d
(repo.or.cz/tinycc.git, 2026-08-05), allowing for the `-` → `_` renames this
project made to some filenames.

  tinycc/    312 files: 239 byte-identical to tinycc's `tests/tests2`,
                        17 tinycc files this project modified,
                        56 not upstream at all — 55 cases written here, plus
                        `fred.txt`, which is output `40_stdio.c` writes when it
                        runs and which was committed by accident.

  pp_tcc/     51 files: 46 byte-identical to tinycc's `tests/pp`,
                        2 modified here (`11.c`, `11.expect`),
                        3 written here (`24.c`, `24.expect`,
                        `24_include_in_call.h`).

The cases written here use upstream's conventions — `NN_name.c` beside
`NN_name.expect`, and `NN+_name.c` for a companion translation unit — because
`tests/toyos.rs` discovers all of them by that shape.


TinyCC: LGPL-2.1
----------------

TinyCC is distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1
(its `COPYING`, and its README: "TCC is distributed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License"). The imported cases and the modifications made to them
here are under those terms.


