One case is gone, and is not coming back
----------------------------------------

`tinycc/46_grep.c` was deleted on 2026-08-08. It was byte-identical to
upstream's, but upstream inherited it with a header of its own:

    Copyright (C) 1980, DECUS

    General permission to copy or modify, but not for profit, is hereby
    granted, provided that the above copyright notice is included and
    reference made to the fact that reproduction privileges were granted by
    DECUS.

"but not for profit" discriminates against a field of endeavour, so it is not a
free licence by any definition, and it was never TinyCC's to relicense — they
vendored it as a test input the same way we did. It cannot sit in a repository
offered under MIT OR Apache-2.0. It was in `C_SKIP` and had never been run
here: it needs `argc`/`argv` and `FILE*`, neither of which `userland/libc`
provides yet.

Do not re-import it. If a regex case is wanted, write one.
